import ../../site/shaders/hero.dl
import site_fixture.dl

set instance to an instance of website fixture
set view to a new UI view
set view's instance to the address of instance
set state to a new website state
set state's view to the address of view
set state's services to the browser UI service provider
set instance's state to (the address of state) as a pointer
set program to a JSON object containing [JSON text "operation" is "shader"]
set (state's shaders + 0)'s program to program
prepare website shader 0 in (the address of state)
prepare website shader 0 in (the address of state)
require condition ((state's requests' purpose = 4) and (state's requests' next = (0 as a pointer to website request))) reporting "Shader preparation registered duplicate in-flight work"
require condition ((state's shaders + 0)'s loading) reporting "Requested shader preparation has no owner"
require condition ((state's shaders + 1)'s loading = false) reporting "Preparing one scene started another scene"
set pending to state's requests
deallocate pending
free program
close the address of instance
print line "Visible shader preparation owns one request without starting unrelated scenes."
